+# v0.4 multi-engine diagnostics
+
+The v0.4 log distinguishes **sensor source** from **sleep detector**. In addition to RAW/SNAP rows, pay attention to these EVENT reasons:
+
+- `DETECTION_CONFIG` — selected detection engine and shadow-mode setting.
+- `HARD_DEADLINE_SET` — unconditional START + 30 min alarm.
+- `WEAR_SLEEP_CAPABILITY` — whether Health Services exposes `USER_ACTIVITY_ASLEEP`.
+- `WEAR_ACTIVITY_STATE` — state plus both `stateChange` and callback `received` time.
+- `DETECTOR_DECISION` — a detector's own confirmation; `authoritative=true/false` tells whether it may schedule the alarm.
+- `SLEEP_DECISION` — the one decision accepted by the coordinator.
+- `NAP_ALARM_SET` — normal +10 target, hard target, selected target and reason.
+
+The recording `powernap-sessions/20260925-131932-000-false-positive.csv` is intentionally retained because the Legacy HR+ACC detector reports sleep although the user remained awake. It is a benchmark for future detector work, not a passing Legacy regression case.
+
