+## Architectural split
 
-The Samsung flavor is intentionally based on the capabilities common to Galaxy Watch4+: continuous heart rate with IBI plus continuous accelerometer. PPG is not used in v0.1.
+`SensorEngine` and `DetectionEngine` are deliberately independent.
 
-## Why Samsung data are explicitly flushed
+`SensorEngine` controls ACC/HR/IBI acquisition. `DetectionEngine` controls which sleep detector is authoritative for alarm scheduling.
 
-Samsung Health Sensor SDK batches continuous samples after the display turns off. Power Nap cannot wait for the normal batch interval, so `SamsungHealthSensorSource` calls `flush()` on HR and accelerometer trackers every 5 seconds while waiting for sleep.
+The current detection choices are:
 
-The detector processes the timestamps belonging to the samples and estimates the onset retrospectively. Therefore the timer is not `callback time + 10 minutes`; it is `estimated sleep onset + 10 minutes`.
+- `AUTO`
+- `WEAR_OS_SLEEP`
+- `LEGACY_HR_ACC`
 
-## Detector features in v0.1
+Legacy can continue in shadow mode while Wear OS is authoritative, giving us side-by-side detector decisions in one CSV session.
 
-* delta-vector wrist movement derived from accelerometer samples,
-* 30-second motion RMS,
-* current median HR versus awake baseline,
-* HR linear slope,
-* IBI-derived RMSSD when Samsung IBI is available,
-* prolonged immobility fallback,
-* candidate/confirmation hysteresis.
+## Wear OS detector
 
-The values are starting heuristics only. They should be tuned against labelled Watch4 CSV sessions.
+`WearOsSleepStateDetector` uses `HealthServices.getClient(context).getPassiveMonitoringClient()`.
 
-## Deliberately excluded for now
+Startup sequence:
 
-* N1/N2/N3/REM classification,
-* raw PPG,
-* Samsung Health sleep-history integration,
-* phone companion app,
-* cloud storage,
-* ML model.
+1. query `getCapabilitiesAsync()`;
+2. test `getSupportedUserActivityStates()` for `USER_ACTIVITY_ASLEEP`;
+3. request user-activity info with `PassiveListenerConfig.Builder().setShouldUserActivityInfoBeRequested(true)`;
+4. use `UserActivityInfo.stateChangeTime` as the candidate onset rather than callback receive time.
 
-These are intentionally deferred until real Watch4 sensor traces show where the heuristic fails.
+A reported ASLEEP onset older than one minute before this PowerNap session is treated as stale and ignored.
 
-## Distribution limitation
+## AUTO arbitration
 
-Samsung Health Sensor SDK works for development with Health Sensor Service developer mode. Shipping an app that uses the Samsung SDK requires Samsung partner approval and registration of the final package name and signing certificate. Keep the current `com.example.powernapwatch` package only for prototyping.
+While capability is unresolved, Legacy can run and log but cannot trigger the alarm. If Wear OS ASLEEP is supported, Wear OS becomes authoritative and Legacy remains shadow. If Wear OS is unsupported or its listener fails, AUTO falls back to Legacy.
+
+A Legacy confirmation occurring before the capability result is kept as a pending decision so AUTO can consume it immediately if fallback becomes necessary.
+
+## Alarm invariant
+
+The hard deadline is scheduled before detectors start:
+
+`hard = START + 30 min`
+
+After sleep detection:
+
+`normal = onset + 10 min`
+
+`selected = min(normal, hard)`
+
+Retrospective sleep delivery is handled by waking promptly if `normal` is already in the past. The pure-Java `AlarmDecisionPolicy` contains this logic and is covered by `scripts/test-alarm-policy.sh`.
+
+## Known limitation retained intentionally
+
+The Legacy HR+ACC detector still reproduces the 2026-09-25 quiet-awake false positive. It remains in the project as a reference/fallback detector while enough real nap data is collected to replace or substantially redesign it.
