+-## First run
+-
+-The UI has an engine selector, `Record RAW sensor data`, `Keep RAW until alarm`, and four actions:
+-
+-* `PERMISSIONS` — grants activity, HR, notification and background health/sensor permissions. Background permission is intentionally requested as a separate step.
+-* `EXACT ALARM` — grants special exact-alarm access.
+-* `START` — starts the foreground monitoring session.
+-* `STOP / CANCEL` — stops monitoring or an active wake-up alarm.
+-
+-The state machine is:
+-
+-```text
+-BASELINE -> WAITING_FOR_SLEEP -> SLEEP_CANDIDATE -> SLEEP_CONFIRMED -> NAPPING -> ALARMING -> FINISHED
+-```
+-
+-Once sleep is confirmed, an exact `AlarmManager` alarm is scheduled for:
+-
+-```text
+-estimatedSleepOnset + 10 minutes
+-```
+-
+-The detector deliberately estimates the earlier sleep-onset boundary rather than starting the 10-minute timer at the later confirmation callback. If `Keep RAW until alarm` is OFF, sensor tracking stops after scheduling. If it is ON, ACC/HR/IBI collection continues until the alarm fires so real-world behavior can still be inspected.
