+-+# PowerNap v0.3.0-user-test
+-+
+-+This build switches back from overnight capture to real PowerNap behavior while retaining diagnostic controls.
+-+
+-+## Behavior
+-+
+-+- Alarm is always enabled and scheduled for `estimated sleep onset + 10 minutes`.
+-+- Exact-alarm permission is required for every normal session.
+-+- Sleep candidate confirmation was increased from 45 s to 120 s after two recorded quiet-awake false positives.
+-+- `Keep RAW until alarm` no longer disables the alarm. It keeps ACC/HR/IBI logging alive after sleep detection and closes the monitoring service when the alarm fires.
+-+- `Record RAW sensor data`, sensor-engine selection, permissions, and exact-alarm controls remain visible during field validation.
+-+- Application/UI label is now `Power Nap` rather than `Power Nap Lab`.
+-+
+-+## Replay evidence used for this build
+-+
+-+- Both previously recorded quiet-awake sessions no longer reach `SLEEP_CONFIRMED` with the 120 s confirmation window.
+-+- Replaying the 24/25 Sep real-sleep session with the new default gives approximately:
+-+  - estimated onset: 23:15:24
+-+  - confirmation: 23:17:56
+-+  - resulting alarm target: 23:25:24
+-+- Samsung Health placed sleep onset around 23:14 (screen-derived reference), so this deliberately conservative detector is late rather than early.
+-+
+-+This is still a user-test build, not a medical sleep classifier.
+-diff -ruN '--exclude=powernap-sessions' '--exclude=v0.2.3-nightcapture.patch' '--exclude=.gradle' '--exclude=build' '--exclude=out' /mnt/data/powernap-finalize-src/PowerNap-v0.2.3-nightcapture/IMPLEMENTATION_NOTES.md /mnt/data/PowerNap-v0.3.0-user-test/IMPLEMENTATION_NOTES.md
+---- /mnt/data/powernap-finalize-src/PowerNap-v0.2.3-nightcapture/IMPLEMENTATION_NOTES.md	2026-09-24 18:05:10.000000000 +0000
+-+++ /mnt/data/PowerNap-v0.3.0-user-test/IMPLEMENTATION_NOTES.md	2026-09-25 11:12:27.128492280 +0000
+-@@ -6,7 +6,7 @@
+- 
+- ## Why Samsung data are explicitly flushed
+- 
+--Samsung Health Sensor SDK batches continuous samples after the display turns off. Power Nap cannot wait for the normal batch interval, so `SamsungHealthSensorSource` calls `flush()` on HR and accelerometer trackers every 10 seconds while waiting for sleep.
+-+Samsung Health Sensor SDK batches continuous samples after the display turns off. Power Nap cannot wait for the normal batch interval, so `SamsungHealthSensorSource` calls `flush()` on HR and accelerometer trackers every 5 seconds while waiting for sleep.
+- 
+- The detector processes the timestamps belonging to the samples and estimates the onset retrospectively. Therefore the timer is not `callback time + 10 minutes`; it is `estimated sleep onset + 10 minutes`.
+- 
+-diff -ruN '--exclude=powernap-sessions' '--exclude=v0.2.3-nightcapture.patch' '--exclude=.gradle' '--exclude=build' '--exclude=out' /mnt/data/powernap-finalize-src/PowerNap-v0.2.3-nightcapture/NIGHT_CAPTURE.md /mnt/data/PowerNap-v0.3.0-user-test/NIGHT_CAPTURE.md
